{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And you shall make a cover.</b> Like the form of a lid. Yefet said that it is like לְכַפֵּר עָלָיו (Leviticus 1:4), like כְּסוּי חֲטָאָה a covering of sin (Psalms 32:1). In my opinion, the word לְכַפֵּר עָלָיו is from the root of כֹּפֶר ransom, and this is explicit: וְנָתְנוּ אִישׁ כֹּפֶר נַפְשׁוֹ (below, 30:12), and there it is written לְכַפֵּר עַל נַפְשֹׁתֵיכֶם (ibid. v. 15). The thickness of the cover is not mentioned."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:18.727534047Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}